urnalism. I'm more interested to see if Maria uses her connections to get on somebody else's show, even if only for one segment, to share what her story was going to be about. If she truly had something juicy then she has a duty to share it with the world regardless if she is still at Fox or not. If she doesn't share anything now, then her story must've been nothingburger to begin with. So the ball is now in her court. She couldn't ask for more free publicity than what she is getting now. Time to show your hand, Maria.\n\nBut at the end of the day, much bigger than just Maria, journalists should not be making friends with the administrations they are covering as it becomes a clear conflict of interest and it is obviously hindered their abilities to do their jobs properly. There's a reason companies strongly discourage office romances and transfer people to other teams when their boss is a romantic interest or even family at times.", "author": "RandomDude25", "created": 1788527724367, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Bullet3250", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Hot take, and an unpopular one at that...", "last_comment_created": 1788531778779, "content": "<p>As it relates to Fox firing Maria Bartiromo, this will be an unpopular opinion but although Fox is gay and is nothing but confirmation bias masturbation for holdover Jeb Bush brand of neocons, it's fucking creepy when any of these news personalities have these strange back room buddy buddy relationships with the White House, whether Trump is the guy in the seat or not. It was creepy as fuck when faggots at CNN, NBC, MSNBC and all of them had these little sweetheart relationships with the Obama and Biden administration behind the scenes and then went on TV to their audience to pretend like they were somehow impartial. Journalist have a very important duty to the public that none of them have fulfilled in a very long time. It's just become another industry corrupted by the desire to get clicks and ratings rather than just do honest investigate of journalism. I'm more interested to see if Maria uses her connections to get on somebody else's show, even if only for one segment, to share what her story was going to be about. If she truly had something juicy then she has a duty to share it with the world regardless if she is still at Fox or not. If she doesn't share anything now, then her story must've been nothingburger to begin with. So the ball is now in her court. She couldn't ask for more free publicity than what she is getting now. Time to show your hand, Maria.</p>\n<p>But at the end of the day, much bigger than just Maria, journalists should not be making friends with the administrations they are covering as it becomes a clear conflict of interest and it is obviously hindered their abilities to do their jobs properly. There's a reason companies strongly discourage office romances and transfer people to other teams when their boss is a romantic interest or even family at times.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 8, "score_up": 14, "is_edited": true, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1ATV89yppR", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 133, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8816151, "raw_content": "", "author": "kek_saved_the_world", "created": 1788483470402, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_aut